#: share/html/Admin/Tools/RightsInspector.html:71
msgid ""
"The \"Principal\" and \"Object\" search fields by default work based on\n"
"filtering. For example typing Principal <kbd>arch</kbd> will show\n"
"permissions granted to the user \"Archibald\", the Group \"Monarchs\", the\n"
"custom role \"Researcher\", and so on. You can also filter using other RT\n"
"concepts by providing search terms like <kbd>user</kbd>,\n"
"<kbd>article</kbd>, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: share/html/Admin/Tools/RightsInspector.html:64
msgid ""
"The \"Right\" field lets you specify partial and/or multiple rights\n"
"(e.g. searching <kbd>Ticket</kbd> will match both \"ShowTicket\" and\n"
"\"ModifyTicket\", while <kbd>ShowAsset ShowCatalog</kbd> will show results\n"
"for both rights). Since \"SuperUser\" provides every other right, it will\n"
"also be included in results when applicable."
msgstr ""

